@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+"""jumper.skill_powerdown -- a robot powering down, a keyframed reference learned by imitation.
+
+A one-shot move on the dance machinery, as the gestures are: the environment is
+`tasks/jumper/common/dance/env.py`, and what this directory adds is the clip and
+the numbers.
+
+## The clip
+
+`media/powerdown.npz`, written by `tools/author_skill_clips.py`, whose docstring has how
+the clip is made and checked; `docs/CRABCRAFT_SKILLS.md` has the numbers it passed
+with. It replaces `death`, one of the hand keyframes "World of Crabcraft" played
+where every other move is a rollout of a trained policy.
+
+A stutter as the power fails, then the walking legs give way one at a time --
+each foot slips 40 mm out, lifted and set down rather than slid -- and the
+shell settles onto the floor on its servo housings, the base origin 39 mm up.
+The claws go limp and are set down ahead and out with the pincers fallen open.
+Held from 2.05 to 3.20 s. Then the claws come back, the body rises, the feet
+step back in two diagonal pairs, and it stands. From the `HOME` footprint the
+shell cannot reach the floor: the knees meet their stops 45 mm down with the
+shell still 25 mm above it.
+
+The clip begins at `HOME` and ends with a lead-out back to it and half a second
+standing there, 5.68 s in all, so it starts and ends where the walking policy
+stands. The game plays a window of it: collapse from 0.30 s, down 1.60 s, settled
+2.05 to 3.20 s, rising 3.60 s, back by 4.76 s.
+
+There is no music, and nothing to export a performance video with: export with
+`--no-video`.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from ...registry import register
+from ..common.assets import JUMPER_ASSETS
+
+register(
+    id="jumper.skill_powerdown",
+    assets=JUMPER_ASSETS,
+    description="jumper hexapod imitating crabcraft's power-down, its death; the clip is "
+                "committed in tasks/jumper/skill_powerdown/media/",
+    tags=("imitation", "jumper", "skill", "flat"),
+)
